From c5638cdbacdcae5014c4ef2d52cc5f73b2ab58ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RDoom <171243930+aeon1911@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 10:04:46 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 53/63] Switch: mallocs of up to 1 KB from the object pool

Console test of 6bba77e33 (Lexicon slaughter + Brutal, ~2000 actors): the
object pool took the horde tic from 16-25 ms to 11-12.6 ms (37-55 fps),
but the game thread still spent ~2.8 ms per frame in ~1500 newlib
malloc/free calls. malloc, free, realloc, calloc and malloc_usable_size are
now wrapped for every thread: blocks of up to 1 KB come from the size-class
pool (libnx mutex, never the wrapped functions inside), anything else and
whatever newlib allocates internally stays with newlib. Ryujinx horde:
heap time per frame 1.1 -> 0.22 ms.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
